<p>The 2018 introduction of the first retina MacBook Air <a href="https://daringfireball.net/2018/11/the_2018_retina_macbook_air">was an interesting event</a>. I noted at the time that it was conspicuous how seldom Apple mentioned “Intel”, despite the fact that all that products introduced ran on Intel chips. Then you <a href="https://daringfireball.net/2018/11/the_2018_retina_macbook_air">look at the specs of that MacBook Air compared to the then-current iPad Pros</a> and you can see why Apple, privately, was seething.</p>

